PHASE 4: RESTORE ALL THREE COLLECTION OPTIONS

Customers must be able to select their preferred package collection arrangement during booking.

Show three clearly differentiated options:

1. Standard Pickup.
2. Priority Pickup.
3. Drop-off.

Do not hide these options in a secondary settings page.

They must be available during shipment booking and before final confirmation.

Standard Pickup

Display:

“Standard pickup”

“Free collection within eligible service areas, with a target of within 24 hours after confirmation.”

Rules:

* Free to the customer where the service is available.
* Subject to approved service coverage.
* Subject to operating hours and available collection capacity.
* Allow customers to select a suitable available pickup date or time window.
* Clearly explain when the next available collection is scheduled.
* Do not promise collection everywhere in Nigeria.

Priority Pickup

Display:

“Priority pickup”

“Request faster collection, with an estimated 1–6-hour window depending on your location and availability.”

Rules:

* Paid service.
* Fee must be calculated using approved business pricing rules.
* Consider collection location, distance, traffic, demand and available collection agents.
* Display the calculated fee before the customer confirms.
* Display the estimated collection window.
* If priority service is unavailable, show it as unavailable rather than allowing a failed booking.
* Do not promise that every priority booking will happen within one hour.
* Create a clear operations priority flag for these bookings.

Drop-off

Display:

“Drop-off”

“Take your package to an approved Swiftvero location.”

Rules:

* Only show active, verified locations.
* Show address and operating hours.
* Allow the customer to select a location.
* Provide clear drop-off instructions.
* Do not show fictional branches or inactive locations.

Scheduling and staff operations

Once the customer selects an option, save the selection against the correct collection job.

The staff operations system must clearly identify:

* Standard pickup.
* Priority pickup.
* Drop-off.

Priority pickups should be easy for authorised staff to identify.

Display booking time, scheduled time, estimated collection window, assigned agent and collection status.

The system should help operations manage the target collection times.

Do not confuse Swiftvero collection with international carrier collection from the Swiftvero facility.

