PHASE 12: TESTING AND ACCEPTANCE REQUIREMENTS

Before reporting completion, test the following scenarios.

Scenario 1: Normal single shipment

* Customer books one shipment.
* Customer selects standard pickup.
* Swiftvero creates a shipment code.
* Pickup appears in operations.
* Package is received and measured.
* Customer receives a quotation.
* Customer retrieves the quotation.
* Customer approves and pays.
* Carrier booking is created.
* Customer tracks the package.
* Customer leaves a review after delivery.

Scenario 2: Priority pickup

* Customer enters an eligible collection address.
* System checks priority availability.
* Customer sees an estimated collection window and fee.
* Customer selects priority pickup.
* Booking is confirmed.
* Operations displays the request as priority.
* Staff can assign the collection.
* Collection events are recorded and the customer is notified.

Test an unavailable priority route too.

Scenario 3: Drop-off

* Customer selects an available drop-off location.
* Location details are shown.
* Customer confirms booking.
* Staff records the package as received.
* The shipment proceeds through inspection and quotation.

Scenario 4: Three destinations

* Customer enters sender information once.
* Customer creates three separate shipments.
* Each shipment has a different destination and recipient.
* Customer selects a shared collection arrangement.
* The system creates one parent booking group and three separate shipment records.
* Each shipment receives its own unique Swiftvero code.
* The customer can see individual quotations.
* Combined payment works only where supported.
* Each shipment can be tracked independently.

Scenario 5: Quote retrieval

* Customer retrieves an outstanding quotation using the shipment code.
* Secure OTP or login is completed.
* Original estimated measurements are visible.
* Verified measurements are visible.
* Customer can approve and pay.
* Customer can request a measurement review.
* Staff can issue a revised quotation.
* Previous quotation versions remain auditable.

Scenario 6: Rewards

* Customer can view cashback.
* Customer can view referral rewards.
* Wallet funds remain separate.
* Balances match the actual ledger.
* Duplicate bonus credit is prevented.

Scenario 7: Customer reviews

* Customer cannot review an undelivered shipment.
* Delivered shipment exposes the review action.
* Customer can submit one review.
* Duplicate submission is prevented.
* Admin can moderate the review.
* Only approved genuine reviews appear publicly.

Test all workflows on mobile and desktop, with light mode and dark mode enabled.

Do not report a test as passed unless it was actually executed.

